WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.980
<i>East China Sea</i>

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.490
Look at all these ships.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.860
They weren't lying when they said 
this was a full-scale operation.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.910
"Victory through overwhelming 
firepower" is America's motto.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.230
But depending on how this goes,

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.700
my first priority is your survival,

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.380
even if it means taking over your Daughter.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.230
I know.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:39.480
I won't do anything reckless.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.810
Did something happen with Gripen?

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.470
"Something"?

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.020
Where did that come from?

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:52.870
My bugs picked up a rather intimate 
conversation between you two last night.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:54.900
I-It wasn't like that...

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.330
Wait, "bugs"?

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.060
That was a joke.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.670
Why are you always so 
excited about everything?

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.120
'Cause I finally get to fly!

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:13.130
We're fighter jets! If we don't fly 
and fight, there's no reason to exist!

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:15.470
Kei...

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:17.830
It's time to get ready.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:18.830
Yeah.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.060
Direct link.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.940
<i>Barbie 01, Control.</i>

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:12.120
<i>A Homeland with No One Home</i>

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.370
<i>Taxi to Alpha Charlie 1.</i>

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:20.650
<i>I hook the nose gear into catapult shaft.</i>

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.800
<i>Then test the flaps and remove 
the engine output limiter.</i>

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.840
<i>After that, I don't touch 
the instruments at all.</i>

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:31.720
<i>I don't touch the stick again until I'm away 
from the carrier and heading into the sky.</i>

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.820
Kei, pull up!

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.400
Checking warning signals.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.120
Normal.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.510
You okay?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.440
Yeah.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.570
<i>Barbie 01, can you hear me?</i>

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.650
Glad to see you made it off the ground.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:06.460
Rhino?

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:07.410
Yes!

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:09.500
It's the first time you're 
seeing me like this, huh?

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:10.960
Let's do good out there today!

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.470
Group 1 just made contact with 
the enemy's forward units.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:18.350
They're falling back and leading 
them to the designated point.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:22.520
<i>Narutani Kei, have you memorized the plan?</i>

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:23.700
Um...

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:29.330
Group 1 is composed of normal fighter jets.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.050
They'll split up the Xi, and then the 
Brawlers in Group 2 will pursue.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.280
We're in Group 3. We'll expand 
the hole the Brawlers open,

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.980
and break through enemy 
lines to secure air superiority.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:41.400
<i>Perfect! You've got it!</i>

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.800
<i>Now we just need to do it.</i>

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.250
She makes it sound so easy.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.110
Let's form up.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:51.180
Follow me.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:04.760
Fire support from the fleet is incoming.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.150
Three...

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.210
Two...

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:07.940
One!

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:09.510
Impact!

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:13.460
Wow...

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:16.490
<i>Be careful. That didn't get a lot of them.</i>

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.260
<i>EPCM level rising.</i>

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:22.170
<i>The enemy is becoming more active.</i>

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.470
<i>They're pursuing Group 1.</i>

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.410
They're not sending in the Brawlers yet?

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.710
<i>The Xi haven't been fully split apart.</i>

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:39.050
<i>If we send them in now,
they'll be attacked from both sides.</i>

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.320
But...

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.490
They're good.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.390
<i>Now it's our turn.</i>

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.610
Target lock on!

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:28.170
Fox 2!

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.080
Kill. Kill.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.150
Splash!

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:56.810
Crap!

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:59.130
Kei, stay in formation.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:00.480
They'll surround you.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:01.720
I know!

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:06.320
But... can we really break through like this?

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.670
Vector zero one five!

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:13.500
The Brawlers found an opening!

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.620
All Barbie fighters, back them up!

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:24.760
We're through.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.680
<i>We made it through the enemy formation.</i>

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:28.290
<i>And we're still alive.</i>

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.420
We were supposed to be first!

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:35.850
Maintaining air superiority is their job.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.840
Our job was just to make an opening, right?

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:43.440
There's no time for talking.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.020
The enemy is still out there.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:48.910
<i>We need to turn around 
and support our allies.</i>

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:52.260
New enemies to our front.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:53.350
Distance: 30.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:56.240
Approaching us from moderate altitude.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.130
Two of them.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.300
Heavy bombers?

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.450
Those are my prey!

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:02.690
Wait!

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:05.240
Those things are too slow to stop us!

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:12.930
Eagle, break!

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.000
<i>Wh-What are those?</i>

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.590
Parasite fighters...

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:20.310
Parasites?

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:24.300
<i>They load up smaller fighters on a 
larger jet and launch them in mid-air.</i>

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:26.310
<i>You can think of them as air-based carriers.</i>

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:29.770
Of all the times and places 
to send those in...

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:35.810
We're going to attack them!

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:37.520
The Brawlers can't stop them all.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:38.180
Okay.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:38.920
<i>Roger!</i>

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.050
<i>I'll go cover the manned fighters!</i>

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.600
Gripen, what's wrong?

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:57.110
EPCM... at incredible intensity.

00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:59.310
And a really weird pattern...

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:00.430
Weird?

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:01.970
Are you okay?

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:02.960
I'm fine.

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.130
I used my shields to cut 
off the signal immediately.

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:07.900
But it made me sick.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.400
What's going on?

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:31.180
They... the Xi are controlling the Brawlers.

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:34.470
The Brawlers' algorithms use the

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:37.500
surrounding EPCM patterns 
to pick their next move.

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:41.660
Which means that if you 
can adjust those patterns,

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:44.350
you can make them do whatever you want.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:45.390
<i>Misidentification...</i>

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:49.600
They can make enemies look like allies, 
and allies look like enemies.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.070
Is that it?

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:54.210
<i>The mission is a failure.</i>

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:55.270
<i>Let's retreat.</i>

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:58.950
<i>Without the Brawlers' support, 
continuing the mission is impossible.</i>

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.150
No, but...

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:01.850
There's no time to waste here!

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.180
They'll kill us all!

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.750
Kei, enemies above us.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.250
From 9 o'clock as well.

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:25.880
I can't get away.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.230
Above us, below, and on both sides...

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.860
The enemy is everywhere!

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:33.230
I can't... I can't die here!

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.810
<i>Narutani Kei!</i>

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:40.180
This way! We're breaking through!

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:41.170
Rhino!

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:05.350
We're alive.

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:09.910
Gripen, you okay?

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:12.160
I took a lot of damage, but I'm okay.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:14.350
But my fuel...

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:16.030
Can we make it to the carrier?

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:17.130
It'll be tough.

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.950
We ended up a long way from the fleet.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.860
<i>Me too. I'm getting fuel warnings.</i>

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:24.820
We need to refuel fast.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.720
Can we call a mid-air refueling tanker?

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:29.020
Nope. Can't get through on the radio.

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:31.290
The EPCM's too bad.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.970
Then we can head for a 
base in Taiwan or Korea...

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:35.040
No way.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.670
They're even father.

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:39.650
What about a Chinese airport?

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:45.150
Shanghai Pudong International Airport.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:47.810
It's close, but...

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:48.920
That's enemy territory.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:51.730
<i>We don't have a lot of other 
choices, though, do we?</i>

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.680
<i>Let's go see what we find.</i>

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:54.680
Okay.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.110
Gripen, watch the surrounding area carefully.

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:58.340
Roger.

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:04.020
I never thought this is how I'd head home.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.970
<i>Mayday, mayday, mayday...</i>

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.480
Pudong Tower, Barbie 01.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:13.010
This is Japan Air Self Defense Force,

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:15.920
low fuel, forced landing, two ships.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:18.210
Not a word from them...

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:20.430
The place seems in good shape, but...

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:26.200
<i>I guess we head for the hangars, huh?</i>

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.270
<i>The weather seems bad.</i>

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:29.690
Yeah.

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:37.760
I'm glad you two are safe.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:40.600
Sorry for dragging you into this.

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:41.940
Don't worry about it.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:44.800
My escape was cut off, too.

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:46.610
But hmm...

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:50.240
There's nothing here. No equipment or fuel.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:54.350
Did they put it all in one place 
somewhere to avoid Xi attacks?

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:55.860
Like in a shelter or something?

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:57.460
Want to take a look?

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:00.260
We can't really fly without 
repairs and fuel, anyway.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:01.430
Sounds good!

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:02.930
Let's go!

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:06.800
Gripen?

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:09.300
What's wrong?

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:10.640
Are you not feeling well?

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:14.440
Kei...

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:15.960
Are you okay?

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.470
I'm fine. Nothing's wrong at all.

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:40.620
Kei...

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:43.900
Is this the country you lived in?

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:46.090
The place you wanted to go home to?

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:48.890
No...

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:50.650
I don't know.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:55.070
It used to be a lot louder, with a 
lot more stuff jammed everywhere.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:14:00.440
It wasn't so quiet, lonely, and white.

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:02.160
White...

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:17.250
Kei...

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:20.170
I'm thirsty.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.260
Want to take a break?

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:25.610
I bet there's some places to eat over there!

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:27.060
The passenger terminal?

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:30.170
We could go back to the 
Daughters and eat rations,

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:32.060
but we need to look around anyway, right?

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:34.780
Yeah. Let's go.

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:02.880
The power's still on.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.090
The air conditioning, too.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:06.660
Is there somebody here after all, then?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:09.460
Are they hiding somewhere?

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:15.690
It's so quiet.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:18.080
This is a nice place.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.870
There's electricity, water, and food, too.

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:22.820
It's clean, and there's so much space.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:25.290
You don't have to worry about the rain.

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:29.220
It feels like we could live here forever.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:31.810
No. Everybody is still fighting.

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:34.700
We need to refuel and head back quickly.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.350
I was just kidding.

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:40.250
Let's split up to search.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:42.660
This place is in such great 
shape that we should be able

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:45.520
to find either supplies or a person quickly.

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:47.480
You couldn't keep this place in this shape

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:49.800
unless somebody was 
maintaining it, after all.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:22.910
The landing lights don't turn on, huh?

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:25.380
We're stuck here tonight, I guess.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:29.960
You'd think, but I actually 
found a place to stay!

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:32.630
Directly linked to the terminal, 
and it comes with a bath and toilet!

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:35.210
Just one room?

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:39.160
I don't want to interrupt your fun, but yeah.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:42.690
I think we need somebody to keep watch.

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:46.450
Until we know who's maintaining this place.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:49.830
Got it. Let's keep watch 
in a three-person shift.

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:51.670
Gripen, is that okay?

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:52.950
Yeah.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:56.360
Okay, I'll take you to your hotel!

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:02.760
How'd the battle go, I wonder?

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:04.880
Hard to say.

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:10.090
It's been a while, so it must've 
reached some kind of conclusion.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.080
Conclusion...

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:14.810
The EPCM in this area is still active.

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:17.760
If the landing force was 
going ahead as planned,

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:21.090
some of them should've been here by now.

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.510
Which means...

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:27.070
Well, we can think about that stuff tomorrow.

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:27.890
We're here.

00:17:41.380 --> 00:17:43.310
What are you doing?

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:46.130
Nothing.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:48.810
Room 405?

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:51.250
I took it from my birthday.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:52.820
Birthday?

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:55.500
It's actually April 5th of this year.

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:56.990
This year?

00:17:56.990 --> 00:17:58.770
Which means you're not even...

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:00.590
I'm zero years old!

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:03.540
If you try anything with me,
 that's a serious crime.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:04.510
I'm not going to!

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:08.470
I'm done. Night.

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:10.920
Hey, at least take a shower.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:15.930
You get some sleep, too.

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:18.550
Your turn at watch is coming soon.

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:19.410
Okay.

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:37.530
What?

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:38.810
Nothing.

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:41.060
Can you see something?

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.360
I like the darkness of night, you know.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:50.080
It's like everything—the people, the towns, 
even me—is going to melt into it.

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:51.570
Melt?

00:18:51.970 --> 00:18:55.870
All the outlines disappear. 
All the boundaries disappear.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:59.530
Everybody gets mixed together,
inside and out.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:05.790
When I was first born, 
somebody took me camping.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:10.540
I can still remember the 
night sky I saw then.

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:20.360
It felt like I was a part of it. 
Or that I was sinking into it.

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:24.630
Like my body was floating in 
the center of the universe.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:29.790
I was a part of the world. Not alone.

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:33.310
It felt like I couldn't 
survive as an individual.

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:39.040
Sorry. I said too much.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:41.600
You should get some sleep.

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:43.500
No, um...

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:47.020
Goodnight, Rhino.

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:49.040
Yeah, goodnight.

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:13.540
Huh?

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:15.760
Rhino?

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:22.610
<i>I'm off to look for fuel.</i>

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.120
<i>If I need you, I'll come get you.</i>

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:25.440
<i>Take your time.</i>

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:29.110
We were supposed to take shifts. That girl...

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.580
Hey, Gripen, wake up.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:35.840
It's morning.

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:41.700
Not feeling well?

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:45.440
My self-examination program 
says everything's normal.

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:48.390
But I feel so out of it.

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.980
Especially since I came to the airport.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:54.140
We should have Yashirodoori-san 
take a look at you ASAP.

00:20:54.970 --> 00:20:57.510
I'll go take a look outside.

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.420
You get some rest.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:02.660
Sorry.

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:13.820
What is that? I heard it yesterday, too.

00:21:28.710 --> 00:21:30.190
Am I imagining it?

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:32.590
Or is it just a ringing in my ears?

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:29.720
Next time on <i>Girly Air Force</i>...

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:33.190
ALT 12: "The Sky I Fly with You."

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:40.010
<i>The Sky I Fly with You</i>

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:37.270
Barbie 01, cleared for take off!
